<quiz>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q01</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q01</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.ENG4.R.11</p><p>Classic context: In Homer&#39;s The Odyssey, Odysseus spends years trying to return home after war. The epic uses a journey pattern involving obstacles, recognition, and the question of what home means after long absence. Contemporary <strong>Passage:</strong> After three years working overseas, Amara returned to a changed city and realized that coming home was not the end of the journey but the last test of it. Which classic pattern influences the contemporary passage?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q01</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>none</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A. A courtroom confession</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>This is not the classic pattern.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>B. The difficult homecoming after long absence</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct. Both texts use return as a test.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>C. A comic mistaken identity scene</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>That is not central here.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>D. A recipe for travel</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>This is unrelated.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q02</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q02</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.ENG4.R.11</p><p>Classic context: The Odyssey asks what home means after long absence. Contemporary <strong>Passage:</strong> Amara expected the streets to recognize her, but new towers had risen where the market used to lean into the river. What transformation occurs?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q02</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>none</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A. The classic pattern disappears entirely.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The homecoming pattern remains.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>B. Amara becomes Odysseus literally.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>She is a contemporary character, not Odysseus.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>C. The city is unchanged.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The city has new towers.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>D. The heroic return becomes a modern experience of changed place and identity.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q03</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q03</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.ENG4.R.10</p><p>Contemporary <strong>Passage:</strong> Her mother opened the door, studied her face, and said, &quot;You have brought the distance with you.&quot; Which paraphrase is accurate?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q03</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>none</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A. Amara&#39;s mother recognizes that Amara&#39;s time away has changed her.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct. This preserves the idea.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>B. Amara&#39;s mother says the trip never happened.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>This contradicts the line.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>C. Amara&#39;s mother refuses to open the door.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>She opens it.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>D. Amara&#39;s mother only comments on luggage size.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The line is figurative.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q04</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q04</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.ENG4.V.01</p><p>Classic influence means:</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q04</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>none</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A. Two texts must have identical plots.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Influence can include transformation.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>B. A newer text cannot change anything from the source.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Adaptations often change sources.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>C. A later text is affected by an earlier text&#39;s patterns, ideas, or structures.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>D. A classic text must be ignored.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The classic pattern matters.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q05</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q05</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.ENG4.R.01</p><p>Contemporary <strong>Passage:</strong> Only then did Amara understand that coming home was not the end of the journey but the last test of it. What is the functional significance of this final sentence?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>ENG4_U02_L06_GP_Q05</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>none</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A. It says the journey never mattered.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>It makes the journey meaningful.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>B. It reframes homecoming as an emotional test rather than simple arrival.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>C. It proves Amara never traveled.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>She worked overseas.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>D. It removes the influence of the classic pattern.</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>It strengthens the homecoming pattern.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
</quiz>

